+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- solo battlegrounds
+// Battlegrounds start with one hero (Zelda.SoloBattlegrounds; BattleGroundQueue testing mode, no
+// premature end). Armies of elite soldiers march: every wave spawns at both bases and runs to the
+// other base, fighting whatever it meets, like a lane in League of Legends - the hero fights with
+// one side. Mini bosses guard the flags (Warsong Gulch) and the five banners (Arathi Basin) and
+// come back a while after they fall. The other side's factions stop being friendly inside.
+bool ZeldaSoloBattlegrounds()
+{
+    static bool const on = sConfig.GetBoolDefault("Zelda.SoloBattlegrounds", true);
+    return on;
+}
